{"id":"mahabharata-9-036","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":36,"title":"षट्त्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 36 · Vinashana and the Saraswati tirthas","summary":{"en":"Balarama comes to Vinashana, where the Saraswati vanishes from hatred of the Shudras and Abhiras, and goes on to Subhumika and other places on the river. He passes the tirthas where the sages performed their austerities, including the Saptasarasvata.","kn":"ಬಲರಾಮ ಶೂದ್ರ-ಅಭೀರರ ದ್ವೇಷದಿಂದ ಸರಸ್ವತಿ ಅದೃಶ್ಯವಾಗುವ ವಿನಶನಕ್ಕೆ ಬಂದು ನದಿಯ ಸುಭೂಮಿಕಾ ಮೊದಲಾದ ಸ್ಥಳಗಳಿಗೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಋಷಿಗಳು ತಪಸ್ಸು ಮಾಡಿದ ಸಪ್ತಸಾರಸ್ವತ ಮೊದಲಾದ ತೀರ್ಥಗಳನ್ನು ದಾಟುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"बलराम विनशन आते हैं जहाँ शूद्रों और आभीरों के द्वेष से सरस्वती लुप्त होती है, और नदी के सुभूमिका आदि स्थानों पर जाते हैं। वे सप्तसारस्वत जैसे उन तीर्थों से गुजरते हैं जहाँ ऋषियों ने तप किया।","te":"బలరాముడు శూద్ర, ఆభీరుల ద్వేషంతో సరస్వతి అదృశ్యమయ్యే వినశనానికి వచ్చి నది వెంట సుభూమిక వంటి చోట్లకు వెళతాడు. ఋషులు తపస్సు చేసిన సప్తసారస్వతం వంటి తీర్థాలను దాటుతాడు.","ta":"பலராமன் சூத்திரர், ஆபீரரின் வெறுப்பால் சரஸ்வதி மறையும் வினசனத்துக்கு வந்து, ஆற்றின் சுபூமிகை முதலிய இடங்களுக்குச் செல்கிறான். முனிவர்கள் தவம் செய்த சப்தசாரஸ்வதம் முதலிய தீர்த்தங்களைக் கடக்கிறான்.","ml":"ശൂദ്രരോടും ആഭീരരോടുമുള്ള വിദ്വേഷത്താൽ സരസ്വതി അപ്രത്യക്ഷയാകുന്ന വിനശനത്തിൽ ബലരാമൻ എത്തുന്നു; പിന്നീട് നദീതീരത്തെ സുഭൂമികം മുതലായ സ്ഥലങ്ങളിലേക്ക് പോകുന്നു. ഋഷിമാർ തപസ്സു ചെയ്ത തീർത്ഥങ്ങളെ, സപ്തസാരസ്വതം ഉൾപ്പെടെ, അദ്ദേഹം കടന്നുപോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.36; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"सारस्वतपर्व","titleEn":"Sarasvata Parva (Balarama's pilgrimage on the Sarasvati)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो विनशनं राजन्नाजगाम हलायुधः ।\nशूद्राभीरान्प्रति द्वेषाद्यत्र नष्टा सरस्वती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, Halayudha came to Vinashana, where the Sarasvati vanished out of spite toward the Shudras and Abhiras."}},{"n":2,"text":"यस्मात्सा भरतश्रेष्ठ द्वेषान्नष्टा सरस्वती ।\nतस्मात्तदृषयो नित्यं प्राहुर्विनशनेति ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because, best of Bharatas, the Sarasvati disappeared there out of spite, the sages always call that place Vinashana."}},{"n":3,"text":"तच्चाप्युपस्पृश्य बलः सरस्वत्यां महाबलः ।\nसुभूमिकं ततोऽगच्छत्सरस्वत्यास्तटे वरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Balarama of great strength touched the water of the Sarasvati there too, and then went to Subhumika on the Sarasvati's fine bank."}},{"n":4,"text":"तत्र चाप्सरसः शुभ्रा नित्यकालमतन्द्रिताः ।\nक्रीडाभिर्विमलाभिश्च क्रीडन्ति विमलाननाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There shining apsaras, ever untiring and fair-faced, play at spotless games."}},{"n":5,"text":"तत्र देवाः सगन्धर्वा मासि मासि जनेश्वर ।\nअभिगच्छन्ति तत्तीर्थं पुण्यं ब्राह्मणसेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, lord of men, gods with gandharvas come every month to that holy tirtha frequented by Brahmins."}},{"n":6,"text":"तत्रादृश्यन्त गन्धर्वास्तथैवाप्सरसां गणाः ।\nसमेत्य सहिता राजन्यथाप्राप्तं यथासुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There gandharvas and troops of apsaras were seen, gathering together, each finding what pleased them, at their ease."}},{"n":7,"text":"तत्र मोदन्ति देवाश्च पितरश्च सवीरुधः ।\nपुण्यैः पुष्पैः सदा दिव्यैः कीर्यमाणाः पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the gods and the ancestors rejoice, with the creepers, again and again strewn with holy, heavenly flowers."}},{"n":8,"text":"आक्रीडभूमिः सा राजंस्तासामप्सरसां शुभा ।\nसुभूमिकेति विख्याता सरस्वत्यास्तटे वरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"That lovely pleasure-ground of those apsaras on the Sarasvati's fine bank, king, is renowned as Subhumika."}},{"n":9,"text":"तत्र स्नात्वा च दत्त्वा च वसु विप्रेषु माधवः ।\nश्रुत्वा गीतं च तद्दिव्यं वादित्राणां च निःस्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing there and giving wealth to Brahmins, Balarama, descendant of Madhu, heard that divine singing and the sound of instruments."}},{"n":10,"text":"छायाश्च विपुला दृष्ट्वा देवगन्धर्वरक्षसाम् ।\nगन्धर्वाणां ततस्तीर्थमागच्छद्रोहिणीसुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the many shadowy forms of gods, gandharvas and rakshasas, Rohini's son then came to the Gandharva tirtha."}},{"n":11,"text":"विश्वावसुमुखास्तत्र गन्धर्वास्तपसान्विताः ।\nनृत्तवादित्रगीतं च कुर्वन्ति सुमनोरमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the austere gandharvas, led by Vishvavasu, make dance, music and song of great charm."}},{"n":12,"text":"तत्र दत्त्वा हलधरो विप्रेभ्यो विविधं वसु ।\nअजाविकं गोखरोष्ट्रं सुवर्णं रजतं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving Brahmins wealth of every kind there, Halayudha gave goats, sheep, cattle, donkeys, camels, gold and silver."}},{"n":13,"text":"भोजयित्वा द्विजान्कामैः संतर्प्य च महाधनैः ।\nप्रययौ सहितो विप्रैः स्तूयमानश्च माधवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He fed the twice-born, satisfied them with their wishes and rich gifts, and Balarama, praised by the Brahmins, set out with them."}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्माद्गन्धर्वतीर्थाच्च महाबाहुररिंदमः ।\nगर्गस्रोतो महातीर्थमाजगामैककुण्डली ॥","meaning":{"en":"From that Gandharva tirtha, the mighty-armed subduer of foes, wearing a single earring, came to the great tirtha Gargasrota."}},{"n":15,"text":"यत्र गर्गेण वृद्धेन तपसा भावितात्मना ।\nकालज्ञानगतिश्चैव ज्योतिषां च व्यतिक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the aged Garga, his soul refined by austerity, learned the course of time and the shifting of the heavenly bodies."}},{"n":16,"text":"उत्पाता दारुणाश्चैव शुभाश्च जनमेजय ।\nसरस्वत्याः शुभे तीर्थे विहिता वै महात्मना ।\nतस्य नाम्ना च तत्तीर्थं गर्गस्रोत इति स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fearful and favorable omens too, Janamejaya, were laid down there by that great soul at the Sarasvati's lovely tirtha, and from his name it is remembered as Gargasrota."}},{"n":17,"text":"तत्र गर्गं महाभागमृषयः सुव्रता नृप ।\nउपासां चक्रिरे नित्यं कालज्ञानं प्रति प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, king, the sages of firm vows constantly attended the fortunate Garga to learn the knowledge of time."}},{"n":18,"text":"तत्र गत्वा महाराज बलः श्वेतानुलेपनः ।\nविधिवद्धि धनं दत्त्वा मुनीनां भावितात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going there, great king, Balarama in white unguents duly gave wealth to the sages of refined souls."}},{"n":19,"text":"उच्चावचांस्तथा भक्ष्यान्द्विजेभ्यो विप्रदाय सः ।\nनीलवासास्ततोऽगच्छच्छङ्खतीर्थं महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having given the Brahmins food of many kinds, the greatly renowned one in blue garments went on to the Shankha tirtha."}},{"n":20,"text":"तत्रापश्यन्महाशङ्खं महामेरुमिवोच्छ्रितम् ।\nश्वेतपर्वतसंकाशमृषिसंघैर्निषेवितम् ।\nसरस्वत्यास्तटे जातं नगं तालध्वजो बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he, the strong palm-bannered Balarama, saw the great Shankha tree on the Sarasvati's bank, tall like great Meru, resembling a white mountain and visited by crowds of sages."}},{"n":21,"text":"यक्षा विद्याधराश्चैव राक्षसाश्चामितौजसः ।\nपिशाचाश्चामितबला यत्र सिद्धाः सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yakshas, vidyadharas, rakshasas of great might, and pishachas of great strength, and thousands of siddhas live there."}},{"n":22,"text":"ते सर्वे ह्यशनं त्यक्त्वा फलं तस्य वनस्पतेः ।\nव्रतैश्च नियमैश्चैव काले काले स्म भुञ्जते ॥","meaning":{"en":"All of them, giving up ordinary food, eat the fruit of that tree from time to time, with vows and disciplines."}},{"n":23,"text":"प्राप्तैश्च नियमैस्तैस्तैर्विचरन्तः पृथक्पृथक् ।\nअदृश्यमाना मनुजैर्व्यचरन्पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having taken up their various observances, they wandered each apart, bull among men, unseen by humans."}},{"n":24,"text":"एवं ख्यातो नरपते लोकेऽस्मिन्स वनस्पतिः ।\nतत्र तीर्थं सरस्वत्याः पावनं लोकविश्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, lord of men, is that tree known in this world, and there is the Sarasvati's purifying tirtha, famed through the world."}},{"n":25,"text":"तस्मिंश्च यदुशार्दूलो दत्त्वा तीर्थे यशस्विनाम् ।\nताम्रायसानि भाण्डानि वस्त्राणि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having given copper and iron vessels and many kinds of cloth at that tirtha to the renowned, that tiger of the Yadus,"}},{"n":26,"text":"पूजयित्वा द्विजांश्चैव पूजितश्च तपोधनैः ।\nपुण्यं द्वैतवनं राजन्नाजगाम हलायुधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"honored the Brahmins and was honored by the ascetics, and Halayudha came to the holy Dvaita forest, king."}},{"n":27,"text":"तत्र गत्वा मुनीन्दृष्ट्वा नानावेषधरान्बलः ।\nआप्लुत्य सलिले चापि पूजयामास वै द्विजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going there and seeing sages in many kinds of dress, Balarama bathed in the water and honored the Brahmins."}},{"n":28,"text":"तथैव दत्त्वा विप्रेभ्यः परिभोगान्सुपुष्कलान् ।\nततः प्रायाद्बलो राजन्दक्षिणेन सरस्वतीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He likewise gave the Brahmins plentiful comforts, and then, king, Balarama went on southward along the Sarasvati."}},{"n":29,"text":"गत्वा चैव महाबाहुर्नातिदूरं महायशाः ।\nधर्मात्मा नागधन्वानं तीर्थमागमदच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having gone not very far, the mighty-armed, greatly renowned, righteous and unfallen Balarama reached the tirtha Nagadhanvan."}},{"n":30,"text":"यत्र पन्नगराजस्य वासुकेः संनिवेशनम् ।\nमहाद्युतेर्महाराज बहुभिः पन्नगैर्वृतम् ।\nयत्रासन्नृषयः सिद्धाः सहस्राणि चतुर्दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is the dwelling of Vasuki, king of serpents, of great splendor, great king, surrounded by many serpents, and there lived fourteen thousand sages and siddhas."}},{"n":31,"text":"यत्र देवाः समागम्य वासुकिं पन्नगोत्तमम् ।\nसर्वपन्नगराजानमभ्यषिञ्चन्यथाविधि ।\nपन्नगेभ्यो भयं तत्र विद्यते न स्म कौरव ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the gods gathered and duly anointed Vasuki, best of serpents, as king of all serpents; and there, Kaurava, there was no fear of serpents."}},{"n":32,"text":"तत्रापि विधिवद्दत्त्वा विप्रेभ्यो रत्नसंचयान् ।\nप्रायात्प्राचीं दिशं राजन्दीप्यमानः स्वतेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"There too, king, he duly gave heaps of jewels to Brahmins and went on toward the east, blazing with his own brilliance."}},{"n":33,"text":"आप्लुत्य बहुशो हृष्टस्तेषु तीर्थेषु लाङ्गली ।\nदत्त्वा वसु द्विजातिभ्यो जगामाति तपस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathing many times with delight at those tirthas, the plough-bearer gave wealth to the twice-born and went on beyond the ascetics."}},{"n":34,"text":"तत्रस्थानृषिसंघांस्तानभिवाद्य हलायुधः ।\nततो रामोऽगमत्तीर्थमृषिभिः सेवितं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Greeting the groups of sages who lived there, Halayudha, Rama, then went to a great tirtha frequented by sages,"}},{"n":35,"text":"यत्र भूयो निववृते प्राङ्मुखा वै सरस्वती ।\nऋषीणां नैमिषेयाणामवेक्षार्थं महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"where the Sarasvati turned back again, facing east, to look on the great-souled sages of Naimisha."}},{"n":36,"text":"निवृत्तां तां सरिच्छ्रेष्ठां तत्र दृष्ट्वा तु लाङ्गली ।\nबभूव विस्मितो राजन्बलः श्वेतानुलेपनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the best of rivers turned back there, the plough-bearer Balarama in white unguents was amazed, king."}},{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"कस्मात्सरस्वती ब्रह्मन्निवृत्ता प्राङ्मुखी ततः ।\nव्याख्यातुमेतदिच्छामि सर्वमध्वर्युसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, why did the Sarasvati turn back and face east there? I wish to hear it all explained, best of Adhvaryu priests."}},{"n":38,"text":"कस्मिंश्च कारणे तत्र विस्मितो यदुनन्दनः ।\nविनिवृत्ता सरिच्छ्रेष्ठा कथमेतद्द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"For what reason was the delight of the Yadu's son aroused there, and how did the best of rivers turn back, best of Brahmins?"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":39,"text":"पूर्वं कृतयुगे राजन्नैमिषेयास्तपस्विनः ।\nवर्तमाने सुबहुले सत्रे द्वादशवार्षिके ।\nऋषयो बहवो राजंस्तत्र संप्रतिपेदिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, in the Krita age, king, the ascetics of Naimisha were holding a very large sacrificial session lasting twelve years, and many sages came to it."}},{"n":40,"text":"उषित्वा च महाभागास्तस्मिन्सत्रे यथाविधि ।\nनिवृत्ते नैमिषेये वै सत्रे द्वादशवार्षिके ।\nआजग्मुरृषयस्तत्र बहवस्तीर्थकारणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having duly stayed through that session, when the twelve-year session at Naimisha ended, many sages came there for the sake of the tirthas."}},{"n":41,"text":"ऋषीणां बहुलत्वात्तु सरस्वत्या विशां पते ।\nतीर्थानि नगरायन्ते कूले वै दक्षिणे तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because of the great number of sages, lord of men, the tirthas along the Sarasvati's southern bank then became like cities."}},{"n":42,"text":"समन्तपञ्चकं यावत्तावत्ते द्विजसत्तमाः ।\nतीर्थलोभान्नरव्याघ्र नद्यास्तीरं समाश्रिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As far as Samantapanchaka, tiger among men, those best of Brahmins settled along the river's bank out of love for the tirthas."}},{"n":43,"text":"जुह्वतां तत्र तेषां तु मुनीनां भावितात्मनाम् ।\nस्वाध्यायेनापि महता बभूवुः पूरिता दिशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As those sages of refined souls offered oblations there and also chanted the Veda loudly, the quarters were filled."}},{"n":44,"text":"अग्निहोत्रैस्ततस्तेषां हूयमानैर्महात्मनाम् ।\nअशोभत सरिच्छ्रेष्ठा दीप्यमानैः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with the sacred fires of those great souls being offered into, the best of rivers shone, blazing all around."}},{"n":45,"text":"वालखिल्या महाराज अश्मकुट्टाश्च तापसाः ।\nदन्तोलूखलिनश्चान्ये संप्रक्षालास्तथापरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, there were Valakhilyas and ascetics who crush with stones, others who use their teeth as mortars, and others who wash everything off."}},{"n":46,"text":"वायुभक्षा जलाहाराः पर्णभक्षाश्च तापसाः ।\nनानानियमयुक्ताश्च तथा स्थण्डिलशायिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were ascetics who live on air, on water, or on leaves, with various vows, and sleepers on bare ground, those sages near the Sarasvati,"}},{"n":47,"text":"आसन्वै मुनयस्तत्र सरस्वत्याः समीपतः ।\nशोभयन्तः सरिच्छ्रेष्ठां गङ्गामिव दिवौकसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"adorning the best of rivers as the gods adorn the Ganga."}},{"n":48,"text":"ततः पश्चात्समापेतुरृषयः सत्रयाजिनः ।\nतेऽवकाशं न ददृशुः कुरुक्षेत्रे महाव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Afterward sages performing sacrificial sessions arrived, men of great vows, and they found no room in Kurukshetra."}},{"n":49,"text":"ततो यज्ञोपवीतैस्ते तत्तीर्थं निर्मिमाय वै ।\nजुहुवुश्चाग्निहोत्राणि चक्रुश्च विविधाः क्रियाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then with their sacred threads they marked out that tirtha, offered the fire-oblations and performed various rites."}},{"n":50,"text":"ततस्तमृषिसंघातं निराशं चिन्तयान्वितम् ।\nदर्शयामास राजेन्द्र तेषामर्थे सरस्वती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king of kings, the Sarasvati, for their sake, showed herself to that company of sages, who were disappointed and anxious."}},{"n":51,"text":"ततः कुञ्जान्बहून्कृत्वा संनिवृत्ता सरिद्वरा ।\nऋषीणां पुण्यतपसां कारुण्याज्जनमेजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, Janamejaya, the best of rivers turned back, making many groves, out of compassion for those sages of holy austerity."}},{"n":52,"text":"ततो निवृत्य राजेन्द्र तेषामर्थे सरस्वती ।\nभूयः प्रतीच्यभिमुखी सुस्राव सरितां वरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having turned back for their sake, king of kings, the Sarasvati, best of rivers, again flowed facing west."}},{"n":53,"text":"अमोघा गमनं कृत्वा तेषां भूयो व्रजाम्यहम् ।\nइत्यद्भुतं महच्चक्रे ततो राजन्महानदी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking \"I shall go back to them so my going is not in vain,\" the great river did this great wonder, king."}},{"n":54,"text":"एवं स कुञ्जो राजेन्द्र नैमिषेय इति स्मृतः ।\nकुरुक्षेत्रे कुरुश्रेष्ठ कुरुष्व महतीः क्रियाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, king of kings, that grove is remembered as Naimisheya; in Kurukshetra, best of Kurus, perform great rites."}},{"n":55,"text":"तत्र कुञ्जान्बहून्दृष्ट्वा संनिवृत्तां च तां नदीम् ।\nबभूव विस्मयस्तत्र रामस्याथ महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the many groves there and the river turned back, great-souled Balarama was filled with wonder."}},{"n":56,"text":"उपस्पृश्य तु तत्रापि विधिवद्यदुनन्दनः ।\nदत्त्वा दायान्द्विजातिभ्यो भाण्डानि विविधानि च ।\nभक्ष्यं पेयं च विविधं ब्राह्मणान्प्रत्यपादयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having duly touched the water there too, the Yadu's son gave gifts and various vessels to the twice-born, and offered the Brahmins many kinds of food and drink."}},{"n":57,"text":"ततः प्रायाद्बलो राजन्पूज्यमानो द्विजातिभिः ।\nसरस्वतीतीर्थवरं नानाद्विजगणायुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, Balarama, honored by the Brahmins, went to the best tirtha of the Sarasvati, crowded with groups of many Brahmins."}},{"n":58,"text":"बदरेङ्गुदकाश्मर्यप्लक्षाश्वत्थविभीतकैः ।\nपनसैश्च पलाशैश्च करीरैः पीलुभिस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was adorned with jujube, ingudi, kashmarya, plaksha, ashvattha, vibhitaka, jackfruit, palasha, karira and pilu trees,"}},{"n":59,"text":"सरस्वतीतीररुहैर्बन्धनैः स्यन्दनैस्तथा ।\nपरूषकवनैश्चैव बिल्वैराम्रातकैस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"with trees growing on the Sarasvati's bank, bandhana and syandana trees, with groves of parushaka, bilva and amrataka,"}},{"n":60,"text":"अतिमुक्तकषण्डैश्च पारिजातैश्च शोभितम् ।\nकदलीवनभूयिष्ठमिष्टं कान्तं मनोरमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"with clumps of atimukta and parijata, abounding in plantain groves, delightful, lovely and charming,"}},{"n":61,"text":"वाय्वम्बुफलपर्णादैर्दन्तोलूखलिकैरपि ।\nतथाश्मकुट्टैर्वानेयैर्मुनिभिर्बहुभिर्वृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and thronged with many forest-dwelling sages who feed on air, water, fruit and leaves, and with tooth-mortar and stone-crushing ascetics."}},{"n":62,"text":"स्वाध्यायघोषसंघुष्टं मृगयूथशताकुलम् ।\nअहिंस्रैर्धर्मपरमैर्नृभिरत्यन्तसेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It resounded with the chanting of the Veda, was full of hundreds of herds of deer, and was much frequented by harmless men devoted to dharma."}},{"n":63,"text":"सप्तसारस्वतं तीर्थमाजगाम हलायुधः ।\nयत्र मङ्कणकः सिद्धस्तपस्तेपे महामुनिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Halayudha came to the Saptasarasvata tirtha, where the siddha great sage Mankanaka performed austerity."}}]}]}